# Netcup SCP — Server Management (Power State & Nickname)
#
# Requires: access_token, server_id
# PATCH requests use JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396) — only specified fields are updated.
# Power state changes may be asynchronous; check task status via 05-tasks.http
# if a task UUID is returned in the response.

### 1 — Update Server State (power on / off / restart)
# Changes the power state of the server.
# Possible state values:
#   started   — power on
#   stopped   — power off (graceful shutdown)
#   restarted — reboot
PATCH {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json

{
  "state": "started"
}

### 2 — Change Server Nickname
# Sets a human-readable nickname for the server (display name only).
# Does not affect the actual hostname of the OS.
PATCH {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/merge-patch+json

{
  "nickname": "my-server"
}
